WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.860
- Arguably, the most important
part of a business document

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.780
is its introduction.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.030
It is so important to
from the very beginning,

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.700
capture the interest of your readers,

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.140
also of your viewers if
you're presenting something.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.310
This is exactly what we are
going to talk about today

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:16.440
in this video,

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.440
My name is Heinrich, welcome
to my channel, Firm Learning.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.690
This is the place where I want
to help you become successful

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.760
in the first years of your career.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.350
Today, I want to introduce
you to a framework,

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.573
an introduction framework,

00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:32.080
that is taught in almost
every onboarding program

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.760
of any of the large consulting firms,

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.800
like McKinsey, BCG, or Bain.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.650
I trust this will be important,

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.260
because it's just so versatile.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.410
You can use it for almost
every business document

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.243
that you use.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.220
The first that I want you to understand

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.210
is that good business writing

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.910
is not something that either
comes or does not come to you.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:51.880
Like many other things,

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.190
it's a skill that needs to be
practiced and can be learned.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.320
And for sure, in consulting
onboarding programs

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.900
at the large strategy consulting firms,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.610
this always played a big role.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:06.690
And an important part of
that is the introduction,

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.430
because, compared to
people reading a book,

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:13.010
clearly no one will ever be as excited

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:15.360
to read your business document

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.410
as the person might be excited

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:21.110
just to read their favorite
book, their favorite novel,

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:23.500
that is just filled
with action, excitement,

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.920
or whatever other topic they
are really interested in.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.880
So as a good business writer,

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.390
with your introduction,

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:33.090
you want to create at least a
little bit of this excitement,

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.980
of this interest of your
reader in your document.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.430
So as most good books,

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.740
the introduction should have a beginning,

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.220
a middle part, and an ending.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.800
And there is one framework

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.987
which is very commonly used
and taught in consulting firms,

00:01:47.987 --> 00:01:50.220
and which I believe is at the core

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:52.540
of almost all good introductions,

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.730
and this framework is the framework

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:58.060
of situation-complication-solution.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.570
So let's now go over

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.510
these three fundamental
components of introduction,

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:04.910
and let's start with the situation.

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.450
So the situation is the
start of introduction

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.350
where you briefly describe

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.720
how the situation currently looks like.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.770
So here, you are looking
for a couple of sentences

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:17.890
where you know that other
people will agree to them,

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:20.487
so you know that the people
reading your document will say,

00:02:20.487 --> 00:02:22.790
"Yes, this is exactly the situation

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.010
that we are currently facing.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.360
This is what the status quo,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.180
what this currently looks like."

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.880
So you don't want to go with
something controversial,

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.310
but rather something where you know

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:34.190
that you have the buy-in
of everyone reading this,

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:36.550
just to make sure that
this is captivating,

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.000
and you will have common
grounds with all your audience.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.420
Of course, and this has then true

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.080
for the other parts as well,

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.970
how detailed this is going to be

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.460
will depend on the overall
context of your document.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.580
So if your total
document, your total memo,

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.740
is only two or three pages long,

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.420
probably this whole introduction

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.440
will only be one or two paragraphs,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.540
whereas if your document
is 50 pages, 100 pages,

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.660
or even longer,

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.380
then likely, this introductory part

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.560
can also be one or two
pages or so, or even longer.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.460
What's important for these first sentences

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.640
of your situation part

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.610
is that what you write is captivating

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.520
so it leaves the reader being interested

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:11.390
in what you are saying

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.310
and wanting to understand further

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:15.350
how the situation will evolve,

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:18.320
what you will have to
say about the situation.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.800
So this is this first
part of your introduction.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.680
So let me make a couple of examples

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.330
for what sentences you could
write here for the situation.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.660
Here, I'm looking at my
other screen to read them.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.847
So for instance, you could
write something like,

00:03:29.847 --> 00:03:32.260
"The profit margin of our company

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:36.667
has been steadily declining
over the last five years."

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.160
That seems interesting.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:40.580
So what do we do about this, right?

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:41.957
This is then the next question,

00:03:41.957 --> 00:03:43.450
how this will be, maybe,

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.940
hopefully of interest to your readers.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.898
Or next, "The public health crisis

00:03:47.898 --> 00:03:50.120
our world is currently facing

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.120
created a significant impact
on our everyday life."

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.550
So again, an uncontroversial statement

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:58.327
that somehow leaves me asking,

00:03:58.327 --> 00:04:01.160
"Okay, what do we do?
How does this continue?"

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.690
Or next, "YouTube channels
have a great capacity

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:07.460
to teach educational material."

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:09.050
So I hope we all agree with that,

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:11.150
but once again, what does this mean?

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.370
What is the implication of that, right?

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:16.110
So this is exactly the effect
that you want to create.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.030
Start with something uncontroversial,

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.600
and then build, based on that.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:20.900
So before we now continue,

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:24.260
let me introduce you to the
